    },
    {
      "text": "Break matzo into pieces in a bowl; cover with hot water and soak until matzo just begins to soften, about 30 to 60 seconds. Drain and squeeze out water; set matzo aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IG5SE2XtAW5q5bGyoaBjxpD9DqI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/16045-matzo-brei-DDMFS-step-02-a4b030adcb214dd39aad4cbc69656e53.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/16045/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beat egg, salt, and pepper together in a small bowl until fluffy; mix in matzo.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/tw0RccrRBhGxx2NGSL8Xd8I7huQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/16045-matzo-brei-DDMFS-step-03-86ef610020f44e13ba6efb574543a7da.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/16045/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat butter or oil in a skillet over medium heat; pour matzo-egg mixture into skillet. Cook until egg is cooked on one side, about 1 minute; flip and cook on other side, about 1 minute more.",
